Got it 👍 I’ll give you a clear, complete setup so your app will:

✔ Auto-select section from link
✔ Check user access
✔ Disable form if not allowed
✔ Still work when user manually selects


---

🎯 OVERALL FLOW

Open link → Get section → Set dropdown → Load data → Check access → Enable/Disable form


---

🧩 STEP 1: LOAD ACCESS LIST (IMPORTANT)

In Screen1.OnVisible (TOP PART)

ClearCollect(
    colAccess,
    'SE Access List'
);

👉 Avoids delegation + faster


---

🧩 STEP 2: AUTO-SELECT SECTION FROM LINK

Still in Screen1.OnVisible:

Set(
    varSectionName,
    Param("section")
);

Set(
    varSelectedSection,
    LookUp(
        'SE Section List',
        Title = varSectionName
    )
);


---

🧩 STEP 3: SET DROPDOWN DEFAULT

Select Dropdown_Section

Default = varSelectedSection.Title


---

🧩 STEP 4: LOAD QUESTIONS + CHECK ACCESS (ONVISIBLE)

Still in Screen1.OnVisible:

// Load questions
ClearCollect(
    colQuestions,
    Filter(
        'SE Question List',
        'Section In-charge'.Value = varSelectedSection.Title
    )
);

// Check access
Set(
    varHasAccess,
    CountRows(
        Filter(
            colAccess,
            Section.Value = varSelectedSection.Title &&
            User.Claims = "i:0#.f|membership|" & User().Email
        )
    ) > 0
);


---

🧩 STEP 5: HANDLE MANUAL SELECTION (IMPORTANT)

👉 Keep your app working even without link

In Dropdown_Section.OnChange:

Set(
    varSelectedSection,
    Dropdown_Section.Selected
);

// Load questions
ClearCollect(
    colQuestions,
    Filter(
        'SE Question List',
        'Section In-charge'.Value = varSelectedSection.Title
    )
);

// Check access
Set(
    varHasAccess,
    CountRows(
        Filter(
            colAccess,
            Section.Value = varSelectedSection.Title &&
            User.Claims = "i:0#.f|membership|" & User().Email
        )
    ) > 0
);


---

🧩 STEP 6: DISABLE FORM

Select your main container (form area)

DisplayMode = If(varHasAccess, DisplayMode.Edit, DisplayMode.Disabled)


---

🧩 STEP 7: OPTIONAL MESSAGE

Add Label:

Text = "You are not authorized to access this section"
Visible = !varHasAccess
Color = Red


---

🧠 IMPORTANT NOTES


---

❗ WHY OnVisible IS REQUIRED

Dropdown.OnChange → NOT triggered when opening via link
OnVisible → ALWAYS triggered


---

❗ WHY WE USE varSelectedSection

Works for BOTH:
✔ Link-based selection
✔ Manual dropdown selection


---

🔗 SAMPLE LINK

https://apps.powerapps.com/play/appId=XXX&tenantId=XXX&section=PR%20PROC


---

🖥️ FINAL BEHAVIOR


---

✅ Authorized user

Open link → PR PROC selected → form enabled → can answer


---

❌ Unauthorized user

Open link → PR PROC selected → form disabled → message shown


